# Feedback widget shared store (Vercel KV / Upstash Redis).
#
# Create a KV / Upstash Redis store in the Vercel dashboard (Storage → create →
# connect to this project). That injects these vars into the deployment.
# Locally, run `vercel env pull` to fetch them into .env.local.
#
# Without these, the /api/feedback route falls back to a per-process in-memory
# store (fine for local dev, NOT shared across users or durable in production).
#
# Either the Vercel KV pair …
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
# … or the Upstash marketplace pair (the route accepts either):
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
